<article class="env-definition" id="03PS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03PS">Definition <span data-tag="03PS">59.33.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\overline{s}$ be a geometric point of $S$ lying over the point $s \in S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>étale local ring of $S$ at $\overline{s}$</em> is the stalk of the structure sheaf $\mathcal{O}_ S$ on $S_{\acute{e}tale}$ at $\overline{s}$. We sometimes call this the <em>strict henselization of $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$</em> relative to the geometric point $\overline{s}$. Notation used: $\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>henselization of $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$</em> is the henselization of the local ring of $S$ at $s$. See Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/04GQ" data-tag="04GQ">10.155.3</a>, and Theorem <a href="/tag/03QL" data-tag="03QL">59.32.8</a>. Notation: $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}^ h$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>strict henselization of $S$ at $\overline{s}$</em> is the scheme $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, \overline{s}}^{sh})$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>henselization of $S$ at $s$</em> is the scheme $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, s}^ h)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>